\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. How shall I sing that majesty
\par Which angels do admire?
\par Let dust in dust and silence lie;
\par Sing, sing, ye heavenly choir.
\par Thousands of thousands stand around
\par Thy throne, O God most high;
\par Ten thousand times ten thousand sound
\par Thy praise; but who am I?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy brightness unto them appears;
\par Whilst I Thy footsteps trace
\par A sound of God comes to my ears,
\par But they behold Thy face.
\par They sing because Thou art their Sun;
\par Lord, send a beam on me,
\par For where heaven is but once begun
\par There alleluias be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Enlighten with faith's light my heart,
\par Inflame it with love's fire;
\par Then shall I sing and bear a part
\par With that celestial choir.
\par I shall, I fear, be dark and cold,
\par With all my fire and light,
\par Yet when Thou dost accept their gold,
\par Lord, treasure up my mite.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. How great a being, Lord, is Thine,
\par Which doth all beings keep!
\par Thy knowledge is the only line
\par To sound so vast a deep.
\par Thou art a sea without a shore,
\par A sun without a sphere;
\par Thy time is now and evermore,
\par Thy place is everywhere.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

